seq v=1 rig=stream program=claude build=2.1.322
# HX-15h (D29, D30): a harness's `turn` record, applied by its stream, is the run's turn.
# `started` opens it stamped as the harness's claim (src=harness conf=claim, by= the tab,
# holder= the claim's holder, hseq= the record's seq), turn_by= naming who opened it; a repeated
# `started` writes nothing, an end of another number ends nothing, and its own end closes it in
# the same stamp. Beside it the screen's busy opens no turn and its rest arms no settle, and the
# transcript's vendor turn names the stream's turn and closes nothing.
stream started 1 by=person
expect open t1 turn par=r1 src=harness conf=claim by=t0000000001 holder=claude-code-alab@4242 hseq=1 turn_by=person @0
expect turn=t1
at 100 see busy
at 200 stream started 1 by=person
at 300 see idle
expect wake=none
at 400 vendor-turn
expect turn=t1
at 5000 expect turn=t1
stream ended 7 done
expect turn=t1
at 6000 stream ended 1 done
expect close t1 turn out=done src=harness conf=claim by=t0000000001 holder=claude-code-alab@4242 hseq=4 @6000
expect turn=none
at 7000 see busy
expect turn=none
at 8000 see idle
expect wake=none
at 12000 expect turn=none
